{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UukqXaC69tvcFExjZXEusG","type":"tool_result","content":"1560\t\n1561\t\n1562\tdef stop_class_enum() -> tuple[str, ...]:\n1563\t    \"\"\"Every class a stop can name, read from the build record schema's own\n1564\t    enum (issue #129) rather than retyped -- STOP_CLASSES already drifted\n1565\t    once (environment arrived in the schema before anything but derive_stop\n1566\t    read it); a second copy is a second place to forget. build's schema is\n1567\t    read, not verify's: verify's own enum is a strict subset (it never\n1568\t    raises environment, cmd_build's own preflight alone).\"\"\"\n1569\t    schema = stage_schema(\"build\")\n1570\t    return tuple(schema[\"properties\"][\"stop\"][\"properties\"][\"class\"][\"enum\"])\n1571\t\n1572\t\n1573\tdef commits_since(root: Path, start_sha: str, end: str = \"HEAD\") -> list[dict]:\n1574\t    \"\"\"(sha, name, email) for every commit after start_sha up to and\n1575\t    including end, first-parent only, oldest first. cmd_build's own call\n1576\t    (start_sha at the invocation, end left at the default HEAD) never sees\n1577\t    a merge in that window, so --first-parent changes nothing there;\n1578\t    issue #128's ledger is the caller that needs it, to walk one branch's\n1579\t    own line without a concurrent merge to main expanding into every\n1580\t    commit main gained meanwhile.\"\"\"\n1581\t    out = git(root, \"log\", \"--first-parent\", \"--reverse\",\n1582\t             \"--format=%H\\x1f%an\\x1f%ae\", f\"{start_sha}..{end}\")\n1583\t    commits = []\n1584\t    for line in out.splitlines():\n1585\t        if not line.strip():\n1586\t            continue\n1587\t        sha, name, email = line.split(\"\\x1f\")\n1588\t        commits.append({\"sha\": sha, \"name\": name, \"email\": email})\n1589\t    return commits\n1590\t\n1591\t\n1592\tdef split_adapter_stdout(stdout: str) -> tuple[str, dict | None]:\n1593\t    \"\"\"(transcript, payload): the adapter's last non-empty stdout line is\n1594\t    its JSON report, and everything before it is transcript, only when\n1595\t    that last line actually parses as JSON. When it does not -- a tool's\n1596\t    own error line printed last on a non-zero exit (issue #86: tenant\n1597\t    zero attest/records/659/verify-01.log, codex's own \"Input exceeds...\"\n1598\t    line, dropped because it was mistaken for an attempted payload) --\n1599\t    nothing here is a report, and the whole stdout is the transcript, so"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e2492c7-2a27-487f-99c4-d4ecc36025b0","uuid":"73fd6948-8628-4948-b37f-cd8dddd7c005","timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:12:28.245Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-153/bin/attavo","content":"\n\ndef stop_class_enum() -> tuple[str, ...]:\n    \"\"\"Every class a stop can name, read from the build record schema's own\n    enum (issue #129) rather than retyped -- STOP_CLASSES already drifted\n    once (environment arrived in the schema before anything but derive_stop\n    read it); a second copy is a second place to forget. build's schema is\n    read, not verify's: verify's own enum is a strict subset (it never\n    raises environment, cmd_build's own preflight alone).\"\"\"\n    schema = stage_schema(\"build\")\n    return tuple(schema[\"properties\"][\"stop\"][\"properties\"][\"class\"][\"enum\"])\n\n\ndef commits_since(root: Path, start_sha: str, end: str = \"HEAD\") -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"(sha, name, email) for every commit after start_sha up to and\n    including end, first-parent only, oldest first. cmd_build's own call\n    (start_sha at the invocation, end left at the default HEAD) never sees\n    a merge in that window, so --first-parent changes nothing there;\n    issue #128's ledger is the caller that needs it, to walk one branch's\n    own line without a concurrent merge to main expanding into every\n    commit main gained meanwhile.\"\"\"\n    out = git(root, \"log\", \"--first-parent\", \"--reverse\",\n             \"--format=%H\\x1f%an\\x1f%ae\", f\"{start_sha}..{end}\")\n    commits = []\n    for line in out.splitlines():\n        if not line.strip():\n            continue\n        sha, name, email = line.split(\"\\x1f\")\n        commits.append({\"sha\": sha, \"name\": name, \"email\": email})\n    return commits\n\n\ndef split_adapter_stdout(stdout: str) -> tuple[str, dict | None]:\n    \"\"\"(transcript, payload): the adapter's last non-empty stdout line is\n    its JSON report, and everything before it is transcript, only when\n    that last line actually parses as JSON. When it does not -- a tool's\n    own error line printed last on a non-zero exit (issue #86: tenant\n    zero attest/records/659/verify-01.log, codex's own \"Input exceeds...\"\n    line, dropped because it was mistaken for an attempted payload) --\n    nothing here is a report, and the whole stdout is the transcript, so","numLines":40,"startLine":1560,"totalLines":3393}}}
